From 246eba87b0793ac3afaba3dbb5a5fbfa9bc197b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:18:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/19] intel: use pre-generated CL shader bindings on Android

Since Mesa 25.x iris/anv (src/intel/shaders) and, in 26.0, blorp
(src/intel/blorp) compile OpenCL C internal shaders at build time with
mesa_clc + vtn_bindgen2, which requires LLVM, clang, libclc,
LLVMSPIRVLib and SPIRV-Tools. None of these are available for the
Android platform build (-Dllvm=disabled).

On Android (and when mesa-clc is left at 'auto'), consume the
vtn_bindgen2 output from <dir>/prebuilt instead and drop the Intel
drivers from with_driver_using_cl. Native builds are unchanged.

The bindings in this commit were generated from mesa-26.0.8 with
android/regen_intel_shaders.sh (LLVM 15.0.7, LLVMSPIRVLib 15.0.0,
SPIRV-Tools v2025.5). They must be regenerated on every Mesa update.

Based on the A16 approach in 9097b4b79e6 ("Fix mesa cl build issue on
android"); float64_spv.h is still generated at build time with
glslang.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1589
Signed-off-by: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
---
